[00:00] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Maintainerr web interface showing "The Best Way to Manage Your Library" and a rule group builder.
AUDIO: 'This is Maintainer, the janitor your media server doesn\'t have. Here\'s the problem it kills. Users request a movie, watch it once, and never touch it again. Half-finished shows sit for years. Your drives fill up, and somehow you\'re the one who decides what to delete.'

[00:13] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Maintainerr "Rules" page displaying various predefined rules like "Stale Movies," "Never-Played Requests," and "Leaving Soon."
AUDIO: 'Maintainer does the deciding for you. Write rules once, and it cleans Plex, Jellyfin, or Emby, plus Radarr, Sonarr, and Seer automatically forever. And the grace period trick that stops your users from yelling at you?'

[00:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'That\'s coming up. The heart of it is a rule builder that reads like plain English. You combine parameters across all your services, Plex watch history, Radarr and Sonarr status, Seer request data, into rules like movies added over'

