AUDIO: 'The GitHub repo holds 2,222 stars with 111 forks, which for a niche this specific, people who run their own Netflix and feel guilty about their storage, is a very healthy install base. Here\'s the full life cycle because the'

[01:53] [scene:info]
VISUAL: A slide titled "The Cleanup Lifecycle" outlining steps: rule matches, visible collection, grace period, then deletion.
AUDIO: 'design is genuinely considerate. When a rule matches a title, Maintainer doesn\'t delete it. It adds it to a collection visible right inside Plex, Jellyfin, or Emby. That collection is the review step. You can inspect it, exclude favorites, and'

[02:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'your users can see what\'s on the chopping block. Then a grace period counts down, a week, a month, whatever you set, giving everyone time to finally watch the thing. Only after that does it delete everywhere at once, the media'

[02:18] [scene:info]
VISUAL: A slide titled "The Cleanup Lifecycle" outlining steps: rule matches, visible collection, grace period, then deletion.
AUDIO: 'server, Radarr or Sonarr, and the original sear request, so nothing ever resyncs back from a stale record. Exclusions are permanent if you want them. Mark the family favorites once and'

[02:31] [scene:terminal]
VISUAL: A terminal window showing a `docker run` command to deploy Maintainerr.
AUDIO: 'no rule ever touches them again. Install as one Docker container, images for both AMD64 and ARM64 from GitHub\'s registry or Docker Hub. Mount a data directory, set your time zone, open port 6246,'

[02:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and the web interface walks you through connecting Plex, the ARR\'s, and Sear. One caveat worth knowing before you deploy, the poster overlay features use a sharp image library which needs a CPU'

[02:57] [scene:terminal]
VISUAL: A terminal window showing a `docker run` command to deploy Maintainerr, with "maintainerr started on :6246".
AUDIO: 'with x86-64 v2 support. On older processors or a misconfigured VM, Maintainer still runs, but overlays switch off. Proxmox users,'

[03:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'set the VM CPU type to host. The whole stack is TypeScript with the data in a single mounted folder, so backup is copying one directory. And here\'s the feature that turns cleanup from a betrayal into a public service, poster'

[03:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'overlays. Titles that are scheduled to leave get a banner stamped right on their poster art, leaving soon with the date inside the apps your users already browse. Nobody needs to check a dashboard. The library'

